bash: add exec-awareness

From: Skye Soss <skye@soss.website>

Check the Linux executability API before interpreting shell input from any
source. EXEC_RESTRICT_FILE is checked for filesystem fds: the script file
argument, files sourced via the . and source builtins, and startup files
(/etc/profile, ~/.bash_profile, ~/.bashrc, --rcfile, $BASH_ENV, $ENV).
EXEC_DENY_INTERACTIVE is checked for stdin, -c command strings, and
commands re-executed by fc.

EXEC_DENY_INTERACTIVE also stops bash from running code taken from the
environment: exported functions are not imported (as in privileged mode),
PS4 is reset to its default (as it is for root), and $BASH_ENV and $ENV
are used as literal paths instead of being expanded, since expansion can
run command substitutions.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
